<title>USA: Continental Air Q4 shr higher.</title>
<headline>Continental Air Q4 shr higher.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Continential Airlines said it earned $47 million, or $0.61 per share in its fourth quarter, fully diluted, compared with $41 million, or $0.55 per share, in the year-ago period.</p>
<p>The earnings beat fully diluted estimates by analysts at First Call of $0.53 per share, the company said.</p>
<p>Financial tables follow in millions of dollars, except per share data:</p>
<p>		  Three Mos Ended  Three Mos Ended	 %</p>
<p>		    Dec 31, 1996	Dec 31, 1995     (Decrease)</p>
<p> Operating Revenue:    1,561		 1,423	    9.7 %</p>
<p> Net Income		   47		    41	   14.6 %</p>
<p> Per share earnings	     0.61	     0.55	10.9 %</p>
<p>		   Year Ended    Year Ended   Increase/</p>
<p>			     Dec 31, 1996  Dec 31, 1995  (Decrease)</p>
<p> Operating Revenue:	     6,360	   5,825	 9.2 %</p>
<p> Net Income			   319	     224	42.4 %</p>
<p> Net Income			4.11		3.15	30.5 %</p>
